(5939677, 863372, 95418, '<td valign="top">Hi from Critique Club.<br/> <br/>You did this picture in a quick way.<br/> <br/>It is not artistic.<br/> <br/>It is real. Just this.<br/> <br/>Ideas:<br/> <br/>1 - Center more the "exit".<br/>2 - Try with more contrast.<br/>3 - Try in B&amp;W with some noise filter.<br/> <br/>Regards<br/> <br/>Oscar</td>', 'Hi from Critique Club. You did this picture in a quick way. It is not artistic. It is real. Just this. Ideas: 1 - Center more the "exit".2 - Try with more contrast.3 - Try in B&W with some noise filter. Regards Oscar', '2010-04-10 21:49:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(5939680, 864066, 95418, '<td valign="top"><br/>Hi from Critique Club.<br/> <br/>Like more or less the image.<br/> <br/>Comments:<br/> <br/>1 - There is a hair there;<br/>2 - Could be a good idea to Sharp and try in B&amp;W;<br/>3 - A black border could be a good idea here and<br/>4 - More contrast can get the water  to be more visible.<br/> <br/>Regards,<br/> <br/>Oscar</td>', 'Hi from Critique Club. Like more or less the image. Comments: 1 - There is a hair there;2 - Could be a good idea to Sharp and try in B&W;3 - A black border could be a good idea here and4 - More contrast can get the water  to be more visible. Regards, Oscar', '2010-04-10 21:53:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(5939765, 863399, 95418, '<td valign="top"><br/>Hello from Critique Club!<br/> <br/>I like your photo more or less  :-(.<br/> <br/>The subject is perfect. <br/> <br/>But is too much close!<br/> <br/>There is a lot of light there.<br/> <br/>Try to adjust to a more dark colors...<br/> <br/>May be you want to blur the image.<br/> <br/>Another idea is to put more sky there. Something like "angels presence".<br/> <br/>Hope you like my ideas.<br/> <br/>Regards,<br/> <br/>Oscar</td>', 'Hello from Critique Club! I like your photo more or less  :-(. The subject is perfect.  But is too much close! There is a lot of light there. Try to adjust to a more dark colors... May be you want to blur the image. Another idea is to put more sky there. Something like "angels presence". Hope you like my ideas. Regards, Oscar', '2010-04-10 23:30:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(5939890, 863854, 14986, '<td valign="top">Great eye to catch this.  I like it alot.</td>', 'Great eye to catch this.  I like it alot.', '2010-04-11 02:06:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(5939996, 863887, 9668, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club! </b> <br/> <br/><b>Conceptual:</b> Awesome. Think it fits this challenge beautifully. Makes me want to walk though and enjoy the ocean on the other side. <br/>"exit to another world" - what makes this seem other worldly? <br/> <br/><b>Composition and Lighting:</b> The lighting here seems a bit dull. Though the lighting on the clouds and surf in the background is interesting, the overcast tones in the foreground don''t give it any emphasis. Maybe at sunrise or sunset with this same frame, you could have captured a totally different scene. <br/> <br/><b>Technical:</b> The first thing that strikes my technical eye is the grainy texture. I think <br/> <br/><b>Overall:</b> Lovely invite into the surf and sun. <br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!   Conceptual: Awesome. Think it fits this challenge beautifully. Makes me want to walk though and enjoy the ocean on the other side. "exit to another world" - what makes this seem other worldly?  Composition and Lighting: The lighting here seems a bit dull. Though the lighting on the clouds and surf in the background is interesting, the overcast tones in the foreground don''t give it any emphasis. Maybe at sunrise or sunset with this same frame, you could have captured a totally different scene.  Technical: The first thing that strikes my technical eye is the grainy texture. I think  Overall: Lovely invite into the surf and sun. ', '2010-04-11 04:44:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(5940222, 863967, 28359, '<td valign="top">What an adventure to get that close. Wonderful image....Congrats!</td>', 'What an adventure to get that close. Wonderful image....Congrats!', '2010-04-11 13:26:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(5940596, 863967, 95418, '<td valign="top">Hi from Critique Club: Fire Exit.<br/> <br/>You know that your photo has a WOW impact of 1.000.000.000 !!!<br/> <br/>But,as you asked, here are some ideas:<br/> <br/>1 - Insert a color border around the image.<br/>2 - The image is a little light. Try to darker it a little.<br/>3 - I believe the subject could be more centered.<br/> <br/>Hope you like the ideas!<br/> <br/>Regards,<br/> <br/>Oscar Burd<br/></td>', 'Hi from Critique Club: Fire Exit. You know that your photo has a WOW impact of 1.000.000.000 !!! But,as you asked, here are some ideas: 1 - Insert a color border around the image.2 - The image is a little light. Try to darker it a little.3 - I believe the subject could be more centered. Hope you like the ideas! Regards, Oscar Burd', '2010-04-11 21:09:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(5940665, 864050, 30982, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Give me a moment with the photograph here... be right back....<br/> <br/>OK, I like the barely there trout (almost typed grout) because I like little surprises in pictures.  The things that you find when you do more than glance and hit a number when voting at DPC, you know?  But I will say that even for me, this is a bit too esoteric or whatever (I''m not good with big words) for a DPC challenge called "Exit".  Granted, there are many meanings of "exit" but other than perhaps this guy is about to be dinner for someone, I''m missing the connection.<br/> <br/>A good abstractish kinda thing, but I personally think you have many other better abstractish kinda things.<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me if you have any questions and I look forward to more of you challenge entries!  :-)</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Give me a moment with the photograph here... be right back.... OK, I like the barely there trout (almost typed grout) because I like little surprises in pictures.  The things that you find when you do more than glance and hit a number when voting at DPC, you know?  But I will say that even for me, this is a bit too esoteric or whatever (I''m not good with big words) for a DPC challenge called "Exit".  Granted, there are many meanings of "exit" but other than perhaps this guy is about to be dinner for someone, I''m missing the connection. A good abstractish kinda thing, but I personally think you have many other better abstractish kinda things. Feel free to PM me if you have any questions and I look forward to more of you challenge entries!  :-)', '2010-04-11 22:11:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(5940693, 862923, 34938, '<td valign="top">Really well done Oliver...congrats on your red...you are on FIRE in 2010!</td>', 'Really well done Oliver...congrats on your red...you are on FIRE in 2010!', '2010-04-11 22:31:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(5940738, 863846, 30982, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>LOL!  Seriously, you made me laugh with the title!  As you well know, though, having a great title doesn''t always guarantee you a great score, especially if it strikes some voters that you''ve used the title to ensure you''ve met the challenge.  As you also know, using inanimate objects doesn''t always fare well either.  Composition is nicely centered, which makes it a bit static (in addition to being inanimate), but you definitely hit the humor note with this one in my opinion!</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! LOL!  Seriously, you made me laugh with the title!  As you well know, though, having a great title doesn''t always guarantee you a great score, especially if it strikes some voters that you''ve used the title to ensure you''ve met the challenge.  As you also know, using inanimate objects doesn''t always fare well either.  Composition is nicely centered, which makes it a bit static (in addition to being inanimate), but you definitely hit the humor note with this one in my opinion!', '2010-04-11 23:03:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(5940770, 863976, 811, '<td valign="top">CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUE<br/>by karmat<br/> <br/>Compositionally, the image is a bit flat/static.  It "fills the frame" but seems a bit too tight to have the eyes "roam" any.  Also, it isn''t quite straight one so it feels tilted even though the words seems straight.<br/> <br/>Technically, the colors are really good.  That bright blue is a great attention getter and the yellow provides a nice contrast.  Also, the focus and exposure looks pretty good, except that resizing may have left some artifacts around the tag and lights.<br/> <br/>Overall, a "cheerful" shot that definitely meets the challenge.  It just lacks the "sophistication" that some of the pictures at the top had.<br/> <br/>If you have any questions, let me know, and best wishes to you in future challenges!<br/> <br/>karma</td>', 'CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUEby karmat Compositionally, the image is a bit flat/static.  It "fills the frame" but seems a bit too tight to have the eyes "roam" any.  Also, it isn''t quite straight one so it feels tilted even though the words seems straight. Technically, the colors are really good.  That bright blue is a great attention getter and the yellow provides a nice contrast.  Also, the focus and exposure looks pretty good, except that resizing may have left some artifacts around the tag and lights. Overall, a "cheerful" shot that definitely meets the challenge.  It just lacks the "sophistication" that some of the pictures at the top had. If you have any questions, let me know, and best wishes to you in future challenges! karma', '2010-04-11 23:26:21.000000', NULL, 0),
